Additional Important Terms

Packet

A packet is a small piece of data sent across a network.

Bandwidth

Bandwidth is the maximum amount of data that can be transferred over a network in a given period of time.

Latency

Latency is the time it takes for data to travel from the source to the destination.

Lower latency usually means better performance.

MAC Address

A unique hardware address assigned to a network interface.

Example:
AA:BB:CC:DD:EE

Public IP

An IP address that is visible on the Internet and can be accessed from outside the local network.

Private IP

An IP address used only inside a local network.

Examples:

* 192.168.x.x
* 10.x.x.x
* 172.16.x.x to 172.31.x.x

Gateway

A gateway is the device that allows your computer to communicate with other networks. In most cases, it is the router.

